2026-09-27 22:17:49 | INFO | P05 | 05. QUERY across related tables with SQL.
2026-09-27 22:17:49 | INFO | P05 | -------------------------------
2026-09-27 22:17:49 | INFO | P05 | 
I want to compare the total number of items sold
for each product group across all stores.

The sales table contains the product group,
number of items sold, and store_id.

The store_id connects each sale to a store
in the stores table.

The result should have one row per product group.

2026-09-27 22:17:49 | INFO | P05 | 
SQL query:

SELECT
    s.product_group,
    SUM(s.items_sold) AS total_items_sold
FROM sales AS s
JOIN stores AS st
    ON s.store_id = st.store_id
GROUP BY
    s.product_group
ORDER BY
    total_items_sold DESC;

2026-09-27 22:17:49 | INFO | P05 | 
Query result:
  product_group  total_items_sold
0       Grocery               153
1          Home               135
2       Apparel                92
3       Outdoor                89
4   Electronics                65
